<li id="guide-step-map-core-foundry-next-to-the-vs-recon-wall-buy"><strong>Core Foundry</strong>, next to the VS Recon wall buy.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-fjord-road-next-to-the-flammefalle-trap"><strong>Fjord Road</strong>, next to the Flammefalle Trap.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-reach-the-flak-gun-near-the-lighthouse-facing-spawn-area-and-place-the">Reach the flak gun near the Lighthouse facing spawn area, and place the Flak Gun Round inside then hit it with the Jotunn Star. If done correctly, the gun should shoot at the Riese robot head in spawn. <ShowOnMap target="areas-lighthouse--eidskallen-landing" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-go-to-the-riese-robot-head-in-spawn-and-hold-interact-with-it-to-get-t">Go to the Riese robot head in spawn and hold interact with it to get the Transmitter. Place the Transmitter inside Tyr's head on the second floor. <ShowOnMap target="areas-eidskallen-landing--tyrs-head" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-check-the-two-blinking-lights-inside-tyr-s-head-the-two-lights-will-bl">Check the two blinking lights inside Tyr's head. The two lights will blink at the same time, then reset, and blink again. Count the number of blinks each time for each light. This will be 2 sets of 2-digit numbers.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-travel-to-core-foundry-and-unlock-the-ascender-with-a-molotov-use-the-">Travel to Core Foundry and unlock the Ascender with a Molotov. Use the Ascender and enter the console to calibrate the Amplitude (right) and Frequency (left) using the numbers from the blinking lights. Enter the first set of numbers which will launch a barrage strike somewhere on the map, then enter the second set of numbers. <ShowOnMap target="core-foundry" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-a-free-wunderbarrage-controller-will-spawn-in-the-ro">If done correctly, a free Wunderbarrage Controller will spawn in the room next to the radio tower. The controller will also become available at crafting tables.</li><li><InlineTool tool="totenreich-wunderbarrage" /> — count the light blinks, keep the pairs on screen.</li>
