<ul>
<li>Uranium 1
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-find-a-fishing-rod-dry-dock-storm-bridge-fishery-island-beacon-island">Find a Fishing Rod (Dry Dock, Storm Bridge, Fishery Island, Beacon Island) <ShowOnMap target="areas-dry-dock--storm-bridge--fishery-island--beacon-island" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-find-a-glowing-green-fish-jumping-in-the-water-at-one-of-the-fishing-l">Find a glowing green fish jumping in the water at one of the fishing location and use the Fishing Rod. Catching the fish will spawn an Irradiated Ravager. <ShowOnMap target="fishing" /></li>
<li>Wait for the next round, and it will appear somewhere on the map, alongside a horde of regular Ravagers. Killing the Irradiated Ravager will drop the Uranium.</li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Uranium 2
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-get-an-arc-xd-and-melee-the-vent-near-stairs-and-zipline-in-core-found">Get an ARC-XD and melee the vent near stairs and Zipline in Core Foundry. With the ARC-XD jump on the boat on the other side and enter the secret room to destroy the barrels and open the Group 935 Genetic Lab.
 <ShowOnMap target="areas-core-foundry--genetic-lab" />
<ul>
<li><em>Note: a free ARC-XD can be picked up in the Eidskallen Square, and it can also be acquired randomly from fishing.</em></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-there-will-be-5-head-jars-marked-a-to-e-around-the-room-look-at-the-co">There will be 5 head jars marked A to E around the room. Look at the corridor next to the locked cell door and note the radioactive symbols beneath the numbers (1 to 5). The numbers match the letter on the jars (A=1 ... E=5) and the radioactive symbols show which jar is needed. Pick up the corresponding jars and place them in the machine next to the cell to get the glowing purple jar.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-interact-with-the-crab-arm-on-the-table-to-pick-up-the-necrospike-use-">Interact with the crab arm on the table to pick up the Necrospike. Use the Necrospike on the cell door to trigger a lockpicking mini-game.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-the-cell-door-will-open-and-the-uranium-can-be-picke">If done correctly, the cell door will open and the Uranium can be picked up. <em>Note: a radio can also be picked up on the ground beneath the bench for a Relic.</em></li>
</ol>
</li>
<li>Uranium 3 - <em>Note: This Uranium can be acquired without the need to build the Jotunn Star or start the main quest.</em>
<ol>
<li>Obtain the Glocke Drop and activate it.
<ul>
<li><em>Note: a free drop is available as part of the beginning steps of the main quest, and it can also be acquired randomly from fishing.</em></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>While active, shoot all the floating zombies to turn on the green light. Keep doing it until all 3 green lights are lit. If done correctly, the Glocke will drop the Uranium.</li>
