<li id="guide-step-map-use-the-wunderbarrage-controller-to-clear-the-debris-on-the-stairs-out">Use the Wunderbarrage Controller to clear the debris on the stairs outside of 02 Building in Dry Dock. Climb the stairs and enter the Machine Workshop. The door to the other side will then automatically open. <ShowOnMap target="areas-dry-dock--machine-workshop" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-place-all-3-uraniums-inside-the-claw-machine-and-interact-with-it">Place all 3 Uraniums inside the claw machine and interact with it.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-record-the-six-existing-tubes-and-choose-three-uranium-placements-that">Record the six existing tubes and choose three Uranium placements that keep the gauge in its target range. Groups connected to Uranium activate; the helper offers layouts from the documented community model. <InlineTool tool="totenreich-uranium" />.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-the-atomkraft-core-will-drop">If done correctly, the Atomkraft Core will drop.

<ul>
<li><em>Note that you cannot sprint while holding the Atomkraft Core and using a zipline or entering Tyr will drop it on the ground.</em></li>
</ul>
</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-place-the-atomkraft-core-on-pallets-next-to-quick-revive-then-turn-on-">Place the Atomkraft Core on pallets next to Quick Revive then turn on the generator in the shed behind the perk. You will need to defend the Atomkraft Core. During the defense, the generator will occasionally require rebooting to progress. <ShowOnMap target="eidskallen-landing" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-once-done-bring-the-charged-atomkraft-core-to-storm-bridge-and-place-i">Once done, bring the Charged Atomkraft Core to Storm Bridge and place it on a barrel. If done correctly, a cutscene will play and the Dravakar Shard will drop next to Tyr's Foot. <ShowOnMap target="areas-storm-bridge--tyrs-foot" /></li>
</ol></div>
<div class="glass-card glass-green"><h2 class="" id="wiki_vegvisir"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Vegvisir<span class="g-tag">🧭 Vegvisir</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-bring-the-shard-inside-the-blodheim-hall-and-place-it-on-the-bonfire-l">Bring the shard inside the Blodheim Hall and place it on the bonfire. Lit the bonfire with the ranged attack of the Jotunn Star. <ShowOnMap target="blodheim-hall" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-get-a-disciple-injection-and-throw-zombies-inside-the-bonfire-note-a-f">Get a Disciple Injection and throw zombies inside the bonfire. <em>Note: a free Disciple Injection can be found in the Eidskallen Stave Church.</em></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-this-should-trigger-a-lockdown-and-spawn-an-necropin">If done correctly, this should trigger a lockdown and spawn an Necropincer HVT.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-after-killing-the-hvt-the-sunstone-can-be-picked-up">After killing the HVT, the Sunstone can be picked up.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-place-the-sunstone-in-the-center-of-eidskallen-stave-church-and-use-th">Place the Sunstone in the center of Eidskallen Stave Church and use the Jotunn Star's range attack on it. A giant circle will spawn above the church with arrows pointing at different runes. <ShowOnMap target="stave-church" /></li>
<li>Runes will spawn around the map, shoot the wooden pile below each rune with the range attack of the Jotunn Star in the order shown in the giant circle, based on the number of arrow points per rune.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-once-done-return-to-tyr-s-head-and-interact-with-the-console-to-start-">Once done, return to Tyr's Head and interact with the console to start the boss fight <ShowOnMap target="tyrs-head" /></li>
</ol></div>
<div class="glass-card glass-red glass-boss"><h2 class="" id="wiki_dravakar_boss_fight"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Dravakar Boss Fight<span class="g-tag">🐉 BOSS</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>
<p><em>Note: Throughout the duration of this fight, if players have completed the Astra Malorum main quest, a power-up called Caltheris's Blessing will drop when all players go down and have no revives left. It will revive the downed player who picks it up.</em></p>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-at-the-start-of-the-fight-dravakar-will-wrestle-with-tyr-in-the-backgr">At the start of the fight, Dravakar will wrestle with Tyr in the background. At certain points, red weak spots will glow on Dravakar; deal damage to these weak spots until they break, which will allow Tyr to gain the upper hand. Otherwise, Dravakar will focus on the players and release an ice attack to one of the three areas in the arena, causing it to freeze temporarily. Three Flammenfalle traps are placed around the arena, which can be used to counter the effects of the ice attacks. <ShowOnMap target="boss-arena" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-after-dealing-enough-damage-to-dravakar-he-will-disable-tyr-for-the-re">After dealing enough damage to Dravakar, he will disable Tyr for the rest of the fight. A Gjallarfrost head will spawn in the middle area, which will attack players when spotted. Stun the Gjallarfrost by throwing a grenade in its mouth, or using the ranged attack of the Jotunn Star, then deal damage with any weapon until it is destroyed. Dravakar will then appear and summon ice shards in rune patterns and shoot them at the players; hide behind covers to avoid the shards, or study the rune patterns to dodge them. During this phase, Dravakar's body will have random red glowing weak spots that can be shot at.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-in-later-phases-dravakar-will-summon-additional-gjallarfrost-heads-on-">In later phases, Dravakar will summon additional Gjallarfrost heads on other sides of the arena. Eventually he will also block off access to the other areas, forcing the player to stay in the middle area with no cover from the ice shard attacks. Continue dealing damage to Dravakar's weak spots until his health bar is depleted.</li>
</ol></div>

