</li>
</ul></div>
<div class="glass-card glass-green"><h2 id="wiki_tyr.27s_power.2Dups"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Tyr's Power-Ups<span class="g-tag">⚡ Power-Ups</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>
<p id="guide-step-map-inside-tyr-s-head-several-lightbubs-can-be-found-above-the-robot-s-mon">Inside Tyr's Head, several lightbubs can be found above the robot's monitor. The lightbubs will display coordinates (such as F 8 or E 2, etc) and the number 75. That number indicates how many zombies need to be killed while being within the coordinates. <ShowOnMap target="tyrs-head" /></p>
<p id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-tyr-s-head-will-flash-green-when-seen-from-the-outsi">If done correctly, Tyr's head will flash green when seen from the outside, and a random Power-Up will spawn inside the head. This can be done once per round.</p></div>
<div class="glass-card glass-gold"><h2 class="" id="wiki_helmets"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Helmets<span class="g-tag">🪖 Helmets</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>
<p><strong>Golden Tide Helm (Blue; Fishing)</strong></p>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-get-the-olaf-s-cod-cranker-fishing-rod">Get the Olaf's Cod Cranker fishing rod. <ShowOnMap target="fishing" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-use-it-at-the-fishing-locations-until-a-special-zombie-called-olaf-cra">Use it at the fishing locations until a special zombie called Olaf, Cranker of Cod spawn wearing a helmet.</li>
<li>Kill the zombie to drop the helmet and pick it up.</li>
</ol>
<p>While wearing the helmet, it should take less time before catching something when fishing, and there will be more chances for better loot like increased Salvage or even Power-Ups. The Golden Tide Helm can be picked up again at Blodheim Hall at no cost.</p>
<p class=""><strong>Kneehigh Helm (Orange; Gnome)</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Obtain Shadow Rift on your weapon.</li>
<li data-guide-step id="guide-step-map-shoot-four-gnome-statues-around-the-map-note-shooting-at-the-statues-s">Shoot four Gnome statues around the map. <strong>Note: shooting at the statues should show a hitmarker and/or a shield icon.</strong>

 <ShowOnMap target="locations-map-shoot-four-gnome-statues-around-the-map-note-shooting-at-the-" label="Show helmets locations on map" />
<ul>
<li id="guide-step-map-between-two-wooden-sheets-next-to-the-catwalk-of-machine-workshop">Between two wooden sheets next to the catwalk of Machine Workshop.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-next-to-a-search-light-on-top-of-a-concrete-building-far-outside-of-ty">Next to a search light on top of a concrete building far outside of Tyr's Foot.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-below-the-painting-on-the-altar-of-eidskallen-stave-church">Below the painting on the altar of Eidskallen Stave Church.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-on-the-catwalk-at-the-top-of-the-lighthouse-when-looking-at-it-from-th">On the catwalk at the top of the lighthouse when looking at it from the Flak gun facing away from the lighthouse.&nbsp;</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-travel-to-loven-s-antiquities-and-pick-up-the-kneehigh-helm-from-the-c">Travel to Loven's Antiquities and pick up the Kneehigh Helm from the counter. <ShowOnMap target="lovens-antiquities" /></li>
</ol>
<p id="guide-step-map-whenever-you-will-crouch-while-wearing-the-kneehigh-helm-you-will-be-t">Whenever you will crouch while wearing the Kneehigh Helm, you will be turned into a Gnome statue. The Kneehigh Helm can be bought up again at Bloodheim Hall for 6000 Essence. <ShowOnMap target="blodheim-hall" /></p>
<div>
<div><strong>Cointoss Helm (Yellow; Power-Up)</strong>
</div>
<ol>
<li>Complete the Tyr's Power-Ups about 15 times (to be confirmed).</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-the-cointoss-helm-should-be-available-within-tyr-s-h">If done correctly, the Cointoss Helm should be available within Tyr's Head. <ShowOnMap target="tyrs-head" /></li>
</ol>
<p>The helmet seemingly increases the frequency of Power-Ups spawn. The Cointoss Helm can be picked up again at Bloodheim Hall at no cost.</p>
<p class=""><strong>Icebane Helm (White; Freeze immunity)</strong></p>
<ol>
<li>Get kills with the Flammenfalle trap:
<ul>
<li>Get 250 kills with the trap itself.</li>
<li>Kill 50 Frost Zombies while inside the trap area of effect with a bullet weapon.</li>
</ul>
</li>
<li>If done correctly, the Icebane Helm should drop on the ground.</li>
</ol>
<p>The helmet will prevent getting frozen during the Special Rounds. When sliding into zombies while wearing the helmet, any zombies hit will be frozen. The Icebane Helm can be picked up again at Bloodheim Hall at no cost.</p>
</div></div>

<div class="glass-card glass-orange"><h2 class="" id="wiki_fishy_fish_bot_trap"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb"><span class="g-title">Fishy Fish Bot Trap<span class="g-tag">🤖 Trap</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>
<ol>
<li id="guide-step-map-get-the-fish-from-the-bucket-located-on-a-shelf-inside-the-shed-next-t">Get the fish from the bucket located on a shelf inside the shed next to the Arsenal at Beacon Island. <ShowOnMap target="beacon-island" /></li>
<li>Get a Shock Charge and wait for a T.E.D.D. Task to spawn.</li>
<li>Place the fish on the T.E.D.D. Task machine and throw the Shock Charge at it then complete the T.E.D.D. Task to the maximum reward.</li>
<li>If done correctly, the fish will drop along aside a piece of the machine.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-bring-both-items-to-the-mount-on-the-wall-across-the-arsenal-in-eidska">Bring both items to the mount on the wall across the Arsenal in Eidskallen Square and hold to build the trap. <ShowOnMap target="eidskallen-square" /></li>
</ol>
<p>The trap costs 2000 Essence and when activated T.E.D.D. will attract the zombies before turning a handful of them into brain-rotted zombies.</p></div>

<div class="glass-card glass-green"><h2 class="" id="wiki_power.2Dup_statues"><label class="g-toggle"><input type="checkbox" class="g-cb" checked><span class="g-title">Power-Up Statues<span class="g-tag">⚡ Statues</span></span><span class="g-chev" aria-hidden="true"></span></label></h2>
<p>There are 7 Power-Up statues around Totenreich giving out the corresponding Power-Ups when shooting them, with two additional statues appearing after the first 7 are activated.</p>
<ul>
<li id="guide-step-map-bonus-point-outside-beacon-island-between-two-wooden-walls"><strong>Bonus Point</strong>: Outside Beacon Island, between two wooden walls. <ShowOnMap target="beacon-island" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-insta-kill-on-a-tombstone-outside-burial-grounds"><strong>Insta-Kill</strong>: On a tombstone outside Burial Grounds. <ShowOnMap target="burial-grounds" /></li>
<li><strong>Double Points</strong>: TBD.</li>
<li id="guide-step-map-nuke-behind-the-riese-robot-head-in-war-factory"><strong>Nuke</strong>: Behind the Riese robot head in War Factory. <ShowOnMap target="war-factory" /></li>
<li id="guide-step-map-full-power-boat-window-inside-dry-dock"><strong>Full Power</strong>: Boat window inside Dry Dock. <ShowOnMap target="dry-dock" /></li>
<li><strong>Max Armor</strong>: TBD.</li>
<li><strong>Max Ammo</strong>: TBD.</li>
<li><strong>Fire Sale</strong>: TBD. <strong>Only available after all the others have been activated.</strong></li>
<li><strong>Random Perk</strong>: TBD. <strong>Only available after all the others have been activated.</strong></li>
</ul></div>

<h1 class="" id="wiki_relics">Relics</h1>
<p>There are 6 Relics that can be unlocked from playing Totenreich, those Relics are then used as gameplay modifiers for Cursed mode.</p>
<p>The Relics are divided into three groups: <strong>Grim</strong>, <strong>Sinister</strong>, and <strong>Wicked</strong>. Each group fill the Cursed Tier bar differently with the Grim Relics filling up a third of the bar, the Sinister Relics filling up two thirds, and the Wicked Relics filling up the entire bar. As such you will need to apply different Relics to reach the desired Tier level.</p>
<ul class="relic-tiers">
  <li><strong>Tier I</strong>: Any 3 <span class="relic-chip grim">Grim</span> — Unlocks Golden Armor (45,000 Essence)</li>
  <li><strong>Tier II</strong>: 2 <span class="relic-chip sinister">Sinister</span> + 2 <span class="relic-chip grim">Grim</span> (example loadout) — Unlocks Ultra Rarity (8,000 Salvage or 17,500 Salvage from default rarity)</li>
  <li><strong>Tier III</strong>: 3 <span class="relic-chip grim">Grim</span> + 2 <span class="relic-chip sinister">Sinister</span> + 1 <span class="relic-chip wicked">Wicked</span> (example) — Unlocks Pack-a-Punch IV (100,000 Essence)</li>
</ul>
<p class="relic-note">Make sure to scroll sideways to see the steps. Higher tiers just need the total difficulty value to match the target fill; swap relics as you discover them.</p>
<div class="relic-grid">
  <div class="relic-section">
    <h2 class="relic-heading grim">Grim Relics</h2>
    <div class="relic-cards">
      <div class="relic-card grim">
        <div class="relic-title">POWER SWITCH <span class="mini-tag">Tactical and lethal equipment randomizes each round</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Start a game in Cursed Mode</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-find-4-wooden-structures-outside-the-map-and-count-the-number-of-deer-">Find 4 wooden structures outside the map and count the number of deer heads for each of them. A scoped weapon makes it easier to spot the structures.  Outside of Eidskallen Landing, when looking at the opening opposite of the Rampage Inducer. <ShowOnMap target="eidskallen-landing" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-outside-of-burial-grounds-right-of-a-mystery-box-spawn-location">Outside of Burial Grounds, right of a Mystery Box spawn location. <ShowOnMap target="burial-grounds" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-outside-of-core-foundry-on-the-left-most-mountain-top-when-looking-fro">Outside of Core Foundry, on the left-most mountain top when looking from the left side of the piled up crates. <ShowOnMap target="core-foundry" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-outside-of-tyr-s-foot-left-of-the-road">Outside of Tyr's Foot, left of the road. <ShowOnMap target="tyrs-foot" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-get-a-combat-axe-and-throw-it-at-a-specific-bear-pelt-hanging-on-the-w">Get a Combat Axe and throw it at a specific bear pelt hanging on the walls of Blodheim Hall in an order based on the number of deer heads (from 1 to 4)  Eidskallen Landing => Pelt surrounded by 3 round shields with another shield on the ground. <ShowOnMap target="blodheim-hall" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-burial-grounds-pelt-with-only-1-shield-on-its-left">Burial Grounds => Pelt with only 1 shield on its left.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-core-foundry-pelt-surrounded-by-4-round-shields">Core Foundry => Pelt surrounded by 4 round shields.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-tyr-s-foot-pelt-surrounded-by-1-shield-on-both-sides">Tyr's Foot => Pelt surrounded by 1 shield on both sides.</li>
          <li>If done correctly, a green portal will spawn on the pelt surrounded by the 4 shields.</li>
          <li>Survive 3 waves as zombies can only be killed with traps.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="relic-card grim">
        <div class="relic-title">??? <span class="mini-tag">TBD</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Reach Round 20</li>
          <li>TBD</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="relic-section">
    <h2 class="relic-heading sinister">Sinister Relics</h2>
    <div class="relic-cards">
      <div class="relic-card sinister">
        <div class="relic-title">STUFFED ELEPHANT <span class="mini-tag">Health regen delay is increased</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Activate Cursed Mode Tier I</li>
          <li>Reach Round 40 without buying or getting any Perks.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-a-yellow-portal-will-spawn-on-a-wall-behind-juggerno">If done correctly, a yellow portal will spawn on a wall behind Juggernog in Fishery Island. <ShowOnMap target="fishery-island" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-shoot-at-4-mr-peeks-eggs-located-around-the-map-and-defeat-the-hvt-tha">Shoot at 4 Mr. Peeks Eggs located around the map and defeat the HVT that will spawn.  On the lower catwalk at the lighthouse in Beacon Island. <ShowOnMap target="areas-lighthouse--beacon-island" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-on-a-window-corner-at-the-house-behind-mule-kick-in-skallen-market">On a window corner at the house behind Mule Kick in Skallen Market. <ShowOnMap target="skallen-market" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-near-tyr-s-foot-outside-of-storm-bridge">Near Tyr's Foot outside of Storm Bridge. <ShowOnMap target="areas-tyrs-foot--storm-bridge" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-on-a-steel-beam-next-to-the-roof-opening-in-the-rk-9-room-at-dry-dock">On a steel beam next to the roof opening in the RK-9 room at Dry Dock. <ShowOnMap target="dry-dock" /></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="relic-card sinister">
        <div class="relic-title">DANCING ARNIE <span class="mini-tag">All Perk-a-Cola machines have been cursed and now give out random Perk-a-Colas</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Activate Cursed Mode Tier I. Do not build the Jotunn Star before Step 4.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-get-the-pot-located-on-the-ground-below-a-wooden-table-behind-mule-kic">Get the pot located on the ground below a wooden table behind Mule Kick in Skallen Market and place it on the fire at the center of Blodheim Hall. <ShowOnMap target="areas-skallen-market--blodheim-hall" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-get-2-items-and-place-them-inside-the-pot-in-blodheim-hall-the-beer-mu">Get 2 items and place them inside the pot in Blodheim Hall:  The beer mug located on a wooden barrel near the barge between Loven's Antiquities and the Arsenal in Eidskallen Square. Return to Blodheim Hall and pour the beer into the pot. <ShowOnMap target="areas-blodheim-hall--lovens-antiquities--eidskallen-square" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-the-chilly-chunks-from-storm-bridge">The Chilly Chunks from Storm Bridge. <ShowOnMap target="storm-bridge" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-with-an-explosive-weapon-shoot-at-the-truck-in-storm-bridge-to-get-a-n">With an explosive weapon shoot at the truck in Storm Bridge to get a new fish can and build the Jotunn Star.</li>
          <li>Get 2 more items to be placed inside the pot:  The red lobster dropped by killing a Necropincer with the Flammenfalle Trap only.</li>
          <li>Round 41+ — Wait for a Special Round and use the fishing spots to catch a unique fish item.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-mr-peeks-will-appear-above-the-pot-in-blodheim-hall">If done correctly, Mr. Peeks will appear above the pot in Blodheim Hall. <ShowOnMap target="blodheim-hall" /></li>
          <li>Kill 100 zombies with the Jotunn Star around Mr. Peeks.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-a-yellow-portal-will-spawn-on-a-wall-above-pack-a-punch-in-fishery-isl">A yellow portal will spawn on a wall above Pack-a-Punch in Fishery Island. <ShowOnMap target="fishery-island" /></li>
          <li>Survive 5 waves while the zombies and HVTs can only take melee damage.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="relic-section">
    <h2 class="relic-heading wicked">Wicked Relics</h2>
    <div class="relic-cards">
      <div class="relic-card wicked">
        <div class="relic-title">AGARTHAN DEVICE <span class="mini-tag">Each round, a different type of zombie will spawn</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Activate Cursed Mode Tier II and one player HAS TO be playing as Richtofen.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-reach-the-urzikstan-and-liberty-falls-room-when-ejecting-from-tyr-s-he">Reach the Urzikstan and Liberty Falls room when ejecting from Tyr's head. <ShowOnMap target="tyrs-head" /></li>
          <li>Urzikstan: Pick the military helmet located on a crate at the bottom of the shelves.</li>
          <li>Liberty Falls: Grab Mr. Peeks from under the bed.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-open-the-cell-in-group-935-genetic-lab-and-pick-up-the-radio-on-the-gr">Open the cell in Group 935 Genetic Lab and pick up the radio on the ground under the bench. <ShowOnMap target="genetic-lab" /></li>
          <li>Activate the Richtofen's Echo of the Damned quest (Round 15+).</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-once-the-echo-of-von-list-has-left-place-the-items-on-the-seat">Once the echo of Von List has left, place the items on the seat. <ShowOnMap target="core-foundry" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-a-red-portal-will-spawn-at-dry-dock">If done correctly, a red portal will spawn at Dry Dock. <ShowOnMap target="dry-dock" /></li>
          <li>Survive 6 waves while the zombies can only be damaged while the players are indoors.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
      <div class="relic-card wicked">
        <div class="relic-title">MUSIC BOX <span class="mini-tag">Enemies only take critical damage</span></div>
        <ol class="steps">
          <li>Activate Cursed Mode Tier II</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-reach-round-60-and-enter-tyr-s-head">Reach Round 60 and enter Tyr's Head. <ShowOnMap target="tyrs-head" /></li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-from-tyr-s-head-window-get-5-critical-kills">From Tyr's Head window, get 5 Critical Kills.</li>
          <li id="guide-step-map-if-done-correctly-mr-peeks-will-laugh-and-a-red-portal-will-spawn-on-a">If done correctly, Mr. Peeks will laugh and a red portal will spawn on a wall in Dry Dock near the Melee Macchiato machine. <ShowOnMap target="dry-dock" /></li>
          <li>Survive 6 waves by holding out lockdowns at specific locations on the map.</li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
